racket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-22T20:32:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the candidates and what are the priorities after TCU fired Sonny Dykes?","description":"Things started well for Dykes, but now the Horned Frogs are looking for a new coach and should have options.","published":"2026-11-22T19:55:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50323301/tcu-candidates-personnel-recruits","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman, Max Olson and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios for Week 12?","description":"Here's what teams from every conference would need to play for their league championship.","published":"2026-11-22T19:15:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No Big Ten football teams in AP top 5 for first time since 2021","description":"A weekend of Big Ten upsets left the conference without a team in the top five of the AP Top 25 college football poll for the first time since 2021.","published":"2026-11-22T20:22:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563638/no-big-ten-football-teams-ap-top-5-first-21","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870711/amare-ferrell","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amare_Ferrell"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Amare Ferrell","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amare_Ferrell","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:34Z","intro":"Amare Ferrell (born June 14, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Indiana Hoosiers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Ferrell attended Columbia High School in Lake City, Florida. He was rated as a three-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Indiana Hoosiers over offers from schools such as Cincinnati, Florida State, Louisville, Kentucky, Miami, and Penn State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman in 2023, Ferrell appeared in all 12 games for the Hoosiers, totaling nine tackles. In the 2024 season opener, he recorded his first career interception against FIU. In week 3, Ferrell recorded an interception in the fourth quarter in a 42–13 win over UCLA. In 2025, Ferrell won the National Championship with the Hoosiers against the Miami Hurricanes."}]}}